{"type":"npc","name":"Wagabago (Illusion, Persecution)","folder":null,"system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":1,"temp":0,"max":1,"details":""},"speed":{"value":25,"otherSpeeds":[],"details":""},"ac":{"value":33,"details":""},"allSaves":{"value":""},"immunities":[],"weaknesses":[]},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":[],"details":""},"level":{"value":13},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>Wagabagos prey on people's fear of change. They taunt their victims with illusions that subvert their hopes for the future, making their pasts seem insurmountable and their dreams impossible to attain. Just before their prey succumbs entirely to despair, they switch tactics, inflating those dreams with unrealistic optimism. They repeat this cycle of despair and hope until their targets become paralyzed by their pasts and terrified at the prospect of the slightest change to their lives.</p><p>Three ever-shifting masks adorn a wagabago's black billowy cloak, which hides their many-eyed limbs. When a wagabago peers into a person's memories, their masks project the faces and voices that are most effective at tormenting their victims.</p><h2>No Future</h2><p>Wagabagos choose as victims people with the greatest abilities to enact change: rulers and commanders in positions of power and young adventurers with glorious destinies before them. By neutralizing these potential difference-makers, they seek to stave off future golden ages and keep the world mired in a stagnant present. Some of those unfortunate people stunted by a wagabago's trickery become pruned futures and other temporal paradoxes.</p>","privateNotes":"","publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Bestiary: Elemental Storm (Pathfinder)","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true}},"resources":{},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":0.941,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"abilities":{"str":{"mod":5},"dex":{"mod":8},"con":{"mod":5},"int":{"mod":6},"wis":{"mod":5},"cha":{"mod":8}},"perception